# Runtime OpenXR wire-protocol ABI pin.
#
# The DisplayXR OpenXR extension headers vendored under
#   Source/DisplayXRCore/Private/Native/openxr/XR_DXR_*.h
# are copied VERBATIM from DisplayXR/displayxr-runtime at the commit below.
# The `abi-guard` CI job (.github/workflows/lint.yml) fetches those headers at
# this ref and fails the build if the vendored copies have drifted — that drift
# is what caused the black-window regression (the Win32 window-binding struct
# grew fields the plugin's hand-mirror lacked) and the rendering-mode stride
# bug (#234).
#
# To adopt new runtime protocol: set this SHA to the new runtime commit, re-copy
# every XR_DXR_*.h header listed in the abi-guard job from displayxr-runtime at
# that SHA into Source/DisplayXRCore/Private/Native/openxr/, and rebuild. Keep
# this as a full 40-char commit SHA (immutable) — not a branch name.
#
# The pin is intentionally independent of the runtime's versions.json co-release
# matrix: this plugin is a downstream consumer of the wire protocol, released on
# its own cadence. This file is the only coupling between the two repos.

# runtime#1486 / #80 (display_info spec v19: the N-view view-configuration type).
#
# Adopted because the runtime made XR_VIEW_CONFIGURATION_TYPE_PRIMARY_STEREO —
# the type this plugin begins its session with — conformant: it now reports
# exactly 2 views and xrEndFrame REJECTS a projection layer with viewCount > 2
# under it (XR_ERROR_VALIDATION_FAILURE). The plugin's submitted view count is
# clamped to 2 to match (DisplayXRMaxSubmittedViews, DisplayXRSession.h); the
# N-view opt-in this header's new enum enables is future work, see
# Docs/DisplayXR/TODO.md.
#
# Diff vs the previous b0e5889 pin, over the seven abi-guard headers: only
# XR_DXR_display_info.h and XR_DXR_view_rig.h change, and both are safe —
#  - display_info 16 -> 19, PURELY ADDITIVE: the
#    XR_VIEW_CONFIGURATION_TYPE_PRIMARY_MULTIVIEW_DXR value (v19),
#    XrDisplayDesktopInfoDXR (v18) and XrEventDataDisplayModeRequestDeniedDXR
#    (v17). No existing struct changed size, layout or field order, and the
#    plugin uses none of the new members yet.
#  - view_rig: one prose comment reworded. SPEC_VERSION unchanged at 3.
# The other five (atlas_capture, win32/cocoa window binding, display_zones,
# local_3d_zone) are byte-identical to the previous pin.
